---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<Layout title="Cloakshape Fighter" active="Hangar">
  <section class="detail-hero"><div class="page-wrap detail-grid"><div class="detail-copy"><p class="kicker">Hangar file 03 // provenance sealed</p><h1>Cloakshape<br />fighter</h1><p class="lede">We acquired it from someone. Morkk flies it when a situation needs to become more direct. The records are incomplete. The scorch marks are not.</p><div class="stamp">CLOAKSHAPE FIGHTER<br />STATUS: HOT / FAST / IMPOLITE<br />PILOT: MORKK, USUALLY<br />OWNERSHIP: A CONVERSATION FOR ANOTHER DAY</div></div><img class="detail-image" src={`${base}media/corridor_breach.jpg`} alt="A dimly lit ship corridor under breach conditions" /></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="page-wrap detail-grid"><div><p class="kicker">Flight notes</p><h2>For when subtlety<br />has already failed.</h2><p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">The Cloakshape is a knife with an engine. It does not carry the crew, the cargo, or the emotional burden of a proper starship. It carries Morkk towards the problem at speed, which has proved useful.</p><div class="spec-table"><div class="spec-row"><span>Primary use</span><strong>Rapid intercept / close support</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Preferred pilot</span><strong>Morkk the Guiltless Predator</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Passenger comfort</span><strong>Not the point</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Acquisition log</span><strong>Redacted by someone who can fly</strong></div></div></div><div class="plate about-card"><p class="kicker">Pilot note</p><h3>“It goes where I point it.”</h3><p style="margin-top:20px">Morkk’s flight philosophy is direct. The rest of us prefer a return vector. The Cloakshape has one, although not always when we need it.</p></div></div></section>
</Layout>
